---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { loadComingSoon, loadIposFile } from '../lib/data';
import { formatUpdated } from '../lib/format';

const { source, updated_at, sample } = loadIposFile();
const pipelineSource = loadComingSoon().source;
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="What IPO Update is, where its data comes from, and its limits.">
  <div class="page-head">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>What this site is, where the data comes from, and what it cannot tell you.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>What this is</h2>
    <p>
      IPO Update is a free, static information page for IPOs and buybacks in the Indian market, with a
      checklist for analysing an issue yourself. There are no accounts, ads or tracking.
    </p>

    <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
    <p>
      This site is for informational purposes only and does not constitute financial advice. IPO
      investments carry risk. Verify all data with NSE, BSE and the registrar before applying. GMP is
      unofficial and volatile.
    </p>

    <h2>Sources</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>IPO cards (dates, price, subscription): {source}, collected automatically from its public page.</li>
      {pipelineSource && <li>Pipeline list on the home page: {pipelineSource} (sebi.gov.in), collected automatically.</li>}
      <li>Last updated: <time datetime={updated_at}>{formatUpdated(updated_at)}</time>.</li>
      <li>GMP, where shown, is entered by hand from unofficial market talk.</li>
      <li>Checklist guidance is written for this site from publicly known analysis practice.</li>
    </ul>
    {
      sample && (
        <p>
          The IPO cards currently show sample data.
        </p>
      )
    }

    <h2>How it updates</h2>
    <p>
      A scheduled job collects public data, checks it, and saves it to the site's repository only when
      something changed. The site is then rebuilt. Data is a snapshot, typically 30 to 60 minutes old,
      never real time.
    </p>

    <h2>Limits</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No allotment status lookup and no applying through this site.</li>
      <li>Subscription figures are snapshots, not live.</li>
      <li>GMP is not automated and may be missing.</li>
      <li>Source pages change; when collection fails, the last good data stays up with its timestamp.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Licence</h2>
    <p>Code is MIT licensed. Written content is CC BY 4.0.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
